---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | konh"
  description="konh is a public notebook for AI product work, agent systems, prompting, memory, and practical engineering notes."
>
  <section class="container article">
    <header class="article-header">
      <span class="meta-line">About konh</span>
      <h1>A public notebook for AI product work.</h1>
      <p>
        konh is where I turn working notes into durable essays: prompting, long-term memory, agent behavior, AI-native
        product systems, and the engineering habits that make those ideas testable.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="article-body">
      <h2>What belongs here</h2>
      <p>
        The site is for material that should survive the project where it started. A staging report may become an
        evaluation pattern. A prompt experiment may become a product rule. A memory-system design may become a reusable
        context-engineering note.
      </p>
      <h2>What does not belong here</h2>
      <p>
        This is not a changelog dump or a polished portfolio. Raw logs can stay in Lark, GitHub, or local docs. The blog
        keeps the parts that can help future product and engineering decisions.
      </p>
      <h2>How it is maintained</h2>
      <p>
        The source is Markdown and MDX in Git. That keeps the archive portable, reviewable, and easy to deploy as static
        HTML.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Email: <a href="mailto:konhcoder@gmail.com">konhcoder@gmail.com</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside class="toc">
      <strong>Focus</strong>
      AI products<br />
      Agent systems<br />
      Prompting<br />
      Memory<br />
      Evaluation<br />
      Contact
    </aside>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
